{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3","id":995674,"title":"How would each Line handle world war 3 ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T09:30:00-07:00","id":995674,"title":"How would each Line handle world war 3 ?","content":"I want to hear some options on how each line would handle world war 3. Lets say world war 3 goes down but no nukes are used its massive land combat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:41:28-07:00","id":995680,"title":"","content":"There are so many more humans with guns, explosives, tanks, rockets, missiles, bombs, airplanes...the list goes on and on. Our species has gotten really good at figuring out different ways of killing each other. In a World War involving massive land armies the only reasoble thing seems to be to get out of the way and survive until the fighting stops. Some would have it easier than others, but everyone would want to get out of the way of even a single military division, which historically speaking consisted of between 10000 to 30000 during the previous World Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","user":"TelperionST","date":". 10-30-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:46:06-07:00","id":995684,"title":"","content":"Werewolves: &quot;So, we basically live in the Shadow now&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages: &quot;Neat. Mind if we join you?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:59:02-07:00","id":995687,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of Order mages will try to influence the Temenos trying to promote peace in humanity minds. But the Seers will try the opposite: promove bellicist ideas in Temenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:40:43-07:00","id":995703,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters: &quot;So, we need to figure out how to deal with the massive upswing in membership? Again?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:05:17-07:00","id":995711,"title":"","content":"TFV: &quot;Hello unchecked government spending.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:12:17-07:00","id":995713,"title":"","content":"Vampires would either start worming their way into arms dealing markets or take a dirt nap and hope it's over by the time they wake up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:52:44-07:00","id":995729,"title":"","content":"The Arisen only stand to profit from human conflict, and while the chaos of war would likely upset quite a few long-term plans and old cults they're nothing if not opportunists. Fighting in the cities allows overt attacks on rivals and open relic thievery, while the emotional turmoil (aided by Sybaris) and loss of faith in political power structures serves only to drive mortals into the waiting arms of cults. If things get bad enough that governments start to fail, expect the Diasporic Code to go out the window as some bold Arisen seek to rule openly, carving out petty kingdoms where you either serve or are forced to survive out in the lawless wastes.<br /> <br /> Civilizations crumble as they always do. Mummies have seen countless apocalypses and weathered them all. Mankind will rebuild again and again, and continue to serve the will of the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:01:18-07:00","id":995734,"title":"","content":"That is a goddamn terrifying motivation for an Arisen antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:42:20-07:00","id":995755,"title":"","content":"Prometheans: &quot;Great, they exchanged pitchforks and torches for bazookas and flamethrowers.&quot;<br /> Demons: &quot;Making a Deal has never been so easy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:57:40-07:00","id":995764,"title":"","content":"An interesting thing to note: for any template that can physically enter another realm of existence, their utility as smugglers is going to be <i>insane</i>. When the only way to get food or water or clean cigarettes (because your city is under siege, or cut off, or in absolute chaos, or rationed by your government) is by ducking into the Shadow or making your way through Trods, you get to control the black market in a way mortals can only dream of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:41:15-07:00","id":995789,"title":"","content":"How would changelings or werewolves handle this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:47:09-07:00","id":995791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995764#post995764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting thing to note: for any template that can physically enter another realm of existence, their utility as smugglers is going to be <i>insane</i>. When the only way to get food or water or clean cigarettes (because your city is under siege, or cut off, or in absolute chaos, or rationed by your government) is by ducking into the Shadow or making your way through Trods, you get to control the black market in a way mortals can only dream of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of that. That's awesome! Criminal Werewolves, Mages, Sin-Eaters and Changelings could thrive. (Beasts too, to a degree).<br /> <br /> But I think WW3 would affect the Shadow a tad negatively, so Werewolves would have their hands full with work, wouldn't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:48:30-07:00","id":995793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995789#post995789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would changelings or werewolves handle this</div> </div> </div> </div>Either join in or just spend more time in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> With the Hedge reacting to pain, hiding out there might not be a good idea but it depends on where the battles are taking place. But at least in first edition they had ample ability to allow them to survive and flourish while the world was in chaos around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995791#post995791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think WW3 would affect the Shadow a tad negatively, so Werewolves would have their hands full with work, wouldn't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Hedge it depends where battles are taking place. Much of World War 2, for instance, was confined to Europe, the Pacific and Northern Africa. But even then, werewolves aren't obligated to keep the Hisil being a peaceful place. That would be impossible, anyways. It can be nice, if you are planning to live there, but just making a big show of dominance can have the same effect. No need to hunt spirits of destruction if they know their place.<br /> <br /> One can look at Basra for a good example of a war-torn locale where werewolves, at least those of a certain tribe, have thrived.<br /> <br /> Many werewolves would probably dive into the fray. With their regeneration, senses, shifting, gifts, and ability to dominate technology they would excel at combat. Unless packs were upset, they would focus on things as they do now. World War 3 wouldn't mean the end of the Claimed or Hosts, for instance, it would just give them opportunity to hide among the chaos. Iron Masters would be able to clearly point out human causes and targets that need to be brought down. Bone Shadows could point out newly formed Wounds and spirits borne of blood. Blood Talons would see it as an opportunity to eliminate long-standing threats and werewolves who they deem to have done wrong.<br /> <br /> The Pure would ironically probably fare the best. Predator Kings are made for that sort of thing, the Ivory Claws are rich and affluent and would likely remain untouched for the most part, the Fire-Touched would have more spirit allies. Bale Hounds would thrive.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolf population would probably rise, with the chaos allowing other totems to take them into lodges or packs without letting them know about the tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-30-2016, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:55:17-07:00","id":995814,"title":"","content":"Just imagine all the squads that would go MIA, assumed to be enemy casualties but in truth killed/captured/used by supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Werewolves have been shown already to occasionally get involved in military operations, both past and present, so they might jump in or be busy trying to protect their territories and mend the Hisil. And it might be decent cover for combatting rivals or enemy factions. Mages... I guess it honestly would depend on the mage themselves. One might be content to try and hide themselves from the world and conflict, while another uses the chaos to cover their own use of magic or experiments on wayward soldiers. Vampires might not be as likely to get openly involved, obviously, but... Again, depends on the individual or group. That being said, the chaos of a city under siege or isolated soldiers would make good targets for hungry blood drinkers. Sin-Eaters might very well find themselves over their heads with unquiet dead, Changelings may be running just as fast as they always have from their pasts in Arcadia, Demons are used to operating under the chaos of mortal action, and so on. <br /> <br /> It might be a fun thing to examine in a Mirrors book if they end up doing any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:17:38-07:00","id":995821,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I feel like Vampires would be more likely to try and push for peaceful amends between nations in this scenario. Massive groups of humans willing to bomb the hell out of cities would hit vampire havens, so torpor won't be able to save them unless they have a dot of protean; and the fact that vampires don't have another realm to run to means that they'd most likely try to fix things because world wars probably go against their instinct to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:20:55-07:00","id":995824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995821#post995821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel like Vampires would be more likely to try and push for peaceful amends between nations in this scenario. Massive groups of humans willing to bomb the hell out of cities would hit vampire havens, so torpor won't be able to save them unless they have a dot of protean; and the fact that vampires don't have another realm to run to means that they'd most likely try to fix things because world wars probably go against their instinct to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, I'm sure many younger Kindred would welcome the change of pace. Elders have had centuries to ingrain themselves into a network of mortal connections, creating a gulf of power and influence between them and the more freshly dead that will never close. With those mortal structures in disarray, the playing field becomes much more even, and nobody will <i>really </i>mourn if a stray artillery round kills the old Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:20:55-07:00","id":995825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995821#post995821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel like Vampires would be more likely to try and push for peaceful amends between nations in this scenario. Massive groups of humans willing to bomb the hell out of cities would hit vampire havens, so torpor won't be able to save them unless they have a dot of protean; and the fact that vampires don't have another realm to run to means that they'd most likely try to fix things because world wars probably go against their instinct to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, I'm sure many younger Kindred would welcome the change of pace. Elders have had centuries to ingrain themselves into a network of mortal connections, creating a gulf of power and influence between them and the more freshly dead that will never close. With those mortal structures in disarray, the playing field becomes much more even, and nobody will <i>really </i>mourn if a stray artillery round kills the old Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:28:00-07:00","id":995857,"title":"","content":"In one of Brian Lumley's Necroscope books one of the vaunted wamphyri, I believe it was Faethor, died during a bombing run in Europe. A wooden beam just struck him while he was asleep and there was nothing he could do to unpin himself.<br /> <br /> Chaos isn't very good for most vampires, I believe a number of books have made a point of showing how scary it can be.<br /> <br /> I do agree that young Kindred might try to take advantage, and not all vampires thrive on order so there would be a lot of hellraisers trying to take advantage also. In real life a lot of people have made their fortunes during wartime, it would be a great opportunity for vampires who have no chance of making a name for themselves to do something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T03:48:20-07:00","id":996016,"title":"","content":"It seems pretty unlikely that no nuclear weapons would get used. They have a utility beyond the mass murder of civilians, especially when one country has a vast proportion of the worlds military power. If there's an American fleet steaming towards you, using nuclear weapons against it is probably your only option; and are the Americans really going to retaliate for your strike against a purely military target with a strike on your homeland? Hopefully not.<br /> <br /> Plus, I gather much of the NATO doctrine for world war 3 was based around using nuclear weapons in a defensive manner. As the Warsaw Pact troops overran your position you'd pull back and detonate nuclear weapons in an attempt to stall them.<br /> <br /> The relevance for here is that while warfare isn't all that great for the Shadow, I'd guess nuclear weapons probably punch wounds into it very easily.<br /> <br /> Imagine that, a huge number of massive wounds out in the middle of the ocean where no one can see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T04:05:19-07:00","id":996019,"title":"","content":"I imagine the wounds are far worse when the nuke is actually used on a city than the tests were. A lot of the problem is all the death and destruction resonance they generate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T04:55:16-07:00","id":996027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996016#post996016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine that, a huge number of massive wounds out in the middle of the ocean where no one can see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably a lot of those already, what with the horrors of the Middle Passage of the slave trade, including the massacre of entire ships worth of 'cargo' to get the insurance money.<br /> <br /> But I think a nuclear strike on ships at sea would be more likely to cause a shoal or barren than a wound. Which would have its own problems.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-31-2016, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:48:13-07:00","id":996038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996027#post996027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's probably a lot of those already, what with the horrors of the Middle Passage of the slave trade, including the massacre of entire ships worth of 'cargo' to get the insurance money.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I think a nuclear strike on ships at sea would be more likely to cause a shoal or barren than a wound. Which would have its own problems. </div> </div> </div>Wounds seem to be caused by atrocities whilst Shoals are caused by severe sorrow and pain, and barrens are caused by the spiritual emptiness of the material world.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you can go from a Wound to a Shoal or barren... it'd be interesting at least. Or hell, combine them; a Shoal with a wound at it's centre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:52:30-07:00","id":996052,"title":"","content":"Somewhere deep in the heart of the Vatican the Pope is meeting with the Shadow Congregation. He asks which Benedicition will summon an Angel, and wheather they could get a few Angels to tell world leaders to knock it off. The Shadow Congregation give the same reason they used for WW1 and WW2, the Pope listens, he thinks, and he makes his decision.<br /> <br /> (I'm assuming the answer isn't &quot;there isn't one&quot;, because that would be boring).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:53:59-07:00","id":996054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996038#post996038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds seem to be caused by atrocities whilst Shoals are caused by severe sorrow and pain, and barrens are caused by the spiritual emptiness of the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Wounds open at sites of atrocities and prolonged cruelty, suffering, and hatred - gulags, torture chambers, or sites that have seen genocide and ethnic cleansing.' While arguably an atrocity I don't think a nuclear strike would fit the others. Perhaps on land, where radiation poisoning and survivors would be a thing, but I think the suddenness of it as well as the distance of whoever's doing it would keep it from becoming a Wound. Compared to one hundred and thirty three people watching each other be murdered in pairs, knowing they will be next, while the perpetrators justify their deeds as being monetarily worth it would leave some marks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if you can go from a Wound to a Shoal or barren... it'd be interesting at least. Or hell, combine them; a Shoal with a wound at it's centre. </div> </div> </div>It says Wounds were once shoals, 'so damaged the Hisil ruptures, opening holes to somewhere else,'<br /> <br /> For what it's worth.<br /> <br /> 'Some upheavals in the Shadow are so terrible they injure the very fabric of the Hisil and disrupt its connection to the material world's resonance, forming a wasteland of nihilistic emptiness called a shoal.'<br /> <br /> 'When the Gauntlet grows unnaturally thick, choking the Hisil of Essence, or the Shadow has been so scoured of Essence by devastation, the rampage of an idigam or the presence of an Ilusah, it results in a spiritual desert called a Barren.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:09:49-07:00","id":996076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=995687#post995687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of Order mages will try to influence the Temenos trying to promote peace in humanity minds. But the Seers will try the opposite: promove bellicist ideas in Temenos.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even the Seers don't want world war III, you can't rule a world of ashes.<br /> <br /> When the nukes fall all the splats die...except the Mummies who arise a thousand years later to go, WTF at the devestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:35:05-07:00","id":996167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996076#post996076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the Seers don't want world war III, you can't rule a world of ashes.<br /> <br /> When the nukes fall all the splats die...except the Mummies who arise a thousand years later to go, WTF at the devestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is &quot;the Praetorians&quot; for $500, Alex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:04:36-07:00","id":996192,"title":"","content":"Might put Demons in a difficult position, the God Machine, as a preserver of the status quo, would probably seek to prevent WW3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:08:12-07:00","id":996194,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the tenseness of the situation would make people more or less likely to sign over their soul.<br /> <br /> Seems like a character like the Mamoulian would fit in just nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:55:29-07:00","id":996247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996192#post996192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might put Demons in a difficult position, the God Machine, as a preserver of the status quo, would probably seek to prevent WW3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not alway's. The god machine did cause world war 1 and 2 to create enough death to make a angel powerful enough to stop a asteroid from hitting the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 10-31-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:22:51-07:00","id":996264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996247#post996247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not away's. The god machine did cause world war 1 and 2 to create enough death to make a angel powerful enough to stop a asteroid from hitting the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have thought an Archmage would have gotten to that for cheaper.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:18:16-07:00","id":996801,"title":"","content":"Demons: &quot;Gentlemen, I think we've just hit the jackpot!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:29:46-07:00","id":997603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996167#post996167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is &quot;the Praetorians&quot; for $500, Alex?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Praetorians are about the fear of warfare, not actual warfare that gets humanity wiped the fuck out like a war with nuclear weapons will.<br /> <br /> Remember that the Seers also have &quot;Protect Humanity&quot; as a tenet.<br /> <br /> The Praetorians are nice and comfy right now where everyone is tip-toeing around conflicts with their &quot;peace-keeping forces&quot; and &quot;armed interventions&quot;, where they can keep the Sleepers afraid and asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:10:52-07:00","id":997705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995674-how-would-each-line-handle-world-war-3?p=996167#post996167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is &quot;the Praetorians&quot; for $500, Alex?</div> </div> </div> </div>The guys that kept the Cold War of ending in a nuclear winter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:45:01-07:00","id":997772,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind, the question was specifically a world war in which nuclear weapons aren't used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}